erpreted through a lens of "well, women are just like that," which erases her individual behavior and intent entirely. I'm not going to agree that this is "just natural" because I don't think the claim holds up, and more importantly, I think it's the kind of unexamined assumption that ends up justifying unfair treatment of specific women in specific situations — including, possibly, the assistant your colleague works with.
